# Documentation System

This project's documentation is installed from
[Docusaurus-Template](https://github.com/The-Running-Dev/Docusaurus-Template).
Re-run the installer with `-Overwrite` to pick up upstream fixes.

## Layout

| Path                              | Owner    | Notes                                        |
| --------------------------------- | -------- | -------------------------------------------- |
| `docs/docs/**`                     | you      | Authored Markdown. Add pages here.            |
| `docs/docs/index.md`               | generated | **Do not edit.** Built from `README.md`.      |
| `docs/docusaurus.config.ts`        | you      | Site title, URL, navbar, broken-link policy.  |
| `docs/sidebar.ts`                  | you      | Sidebar structure.                            |
| `docs/Dockerfile`, `.dockerignore` | template | Local preview only.                           |
| `docs.ps1`                         | template | Local preview entry point.                    |
| `build/*.ps1`                      | template | Homepage generator and documentation gate.    |
| `.config/DocumentationRules.psd1`  | you      | Gate rules. Tune terminology and exclusions.  |
| `.github/workflows/docs*.yml`      | template | Verify, gate, and deploy.                     |

Files marked `template` are replaced wholesale on the next `-Overwrite` install.
Do not edit them — put project-specific settings in `DocumentationRules.psd1`,
`docusaurus.config.ts`, or `sidebar.ts` instead.

## The homepage is generated — never edit it by hand

`docs/docs/index.md` is produced from `README.md` by
`build/ConvertTo-DocumentationHomepage.ps1`. The gate re-runs that generator and
fails if the committed copy differs, so a hand edit is reverted in effect: the
next regeneration overwrites it, and CI fails until it matches.

**To change the homepage, edit `README.md`,** then regenerate:

```powershell
./docs.ps1 -BuildOnly    # regenerates docs/docs/index.md as a side effect
```

Commit `README.md` and the regenerated `docs/docs/index.md` together. A README
change committed without the regenerated homepage fails the gate with
`GeneratedFile: Generated from 'README.md' but the committed copy differs`.

### Known trap: relative links in the README

The generator rewrites the configured `SiteUrl` to `/`, but does **not** rewrite
relative links. A README link that is valid at the repository root breaks once
copied one directory deeper into `docs/docs/index.md`:

```
README.md            See [the guide](docs/guide.md).      valid
docs/docs/index.md   See [the guide](docs/guide.md).      resolves to
                                                          docs/docs/docs/guide.md
```

The gate reports this as a `MarkdownLink` error against `docs/docs/index.md`. In
a README, prefer absolute links (to the code host or the published site) over
repository-relative ones for anything the homepage should reach.

## Running the gate

```powershell
./build/Test-Documentation.ps1                          # whole repository
./build/Test-Documentation.ps1 -Path README.md          # one file or directory
./build/Test-Documentation.ps1 -TreatWarningsAsErrors   # strict
```

The project must be a git repository — the gate locates the repository root by
walking up for a `.git` marker and errors clearly if there is none.

### What it checks

| Rule             | Severity | Meaning                                                       |
| ---------------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `MarkdownLink`   | Error    | Relative link target does not exist on disk.                   |
| `MarkdownAnchor` | Error    | `#fragment` matches no heading in the target document.         |
| `GeneratedFile`  | Error    | A generated file no longer matches its source.                 |
| `Terminology`    | Warning  | Product name cased inconsistently, e.g. `Github` → `GitHub`.   |

Errors fail the run. Warnings are reported and do not block unless
`-TreatWarningsAsErrors` is passed.

External `http(s)`, `mailto`, and site-absolute (`/...`) links are deliberately
out of scope — the gate never makes network calls, and Docusaurus' own
broken-link pass covers site-absolute routes at build time.

### It will not flag your code samples

Fenced blocks, inline code spans, link targets, and bare URLs are blanked before
the rules run, with line and column numbers preserved. A sample that
deliberately shows `Github` or `npm install` is not a finding. If something in
prose is flagged that should not be, add it to `Terminology` or `ExcludedFiles`
in `.config/DocumentationRules.psd1` rather than working around the gate.

## Local preview

```powershell
./docs.ps1              # build the overlay image and serve on :3000
./docs.ps1 -Live        # hot-reload edits under docs/
./docs.ps1 -BuildOnly   # build only, do not serve
```

Requires Docker. The site is built by overlaying `docs/` onto the published base
image, so no local Node install is needed. `docs.ps1` regenerates the homepage on
every run unless `-NoHomepage` is passed.

## CI

- `docs.yml` — the only workflow with triggers; calls the other two.
- `docs-quality.yml` — runs the gate on pull requests. Pure PowerShell, no container.
- `docs-ci.yml` — builds the site, and archives the Pages artifact so the deploy
  path is exercised before merge rather than after.
- `docs-deploy.yml` — deploys to GitHub Pages on push to the default branch.

Enable GitHub Pages with source "GitHub Actions", and mark the docs checks
**required** — otherwise a red run does not block a merge.

## Before you commit documentation changes

1. Edited `README.md`? Regenerate with `./docs.ps1 -BuildOnly` and commit both files.
2. Run `./build/Test-Documentation.ps1` and resolve every Error.
3. Added a page under `docs/docs/`? Check it appears in `docs/sidebar.ts`.
